> You step out from the corridor. The corridor opens onto a broad landing where a great staircase winds up into blackness and sinks down toward a colder, closer dark. The banister is carved with vines that seem, when a Vigil Lamp kindles overhead, to have shifted their coils since you last looked away. From somewhere below rises a faint clatter — not the settling of an old house, but something moving, and moving carelessly. Steps descend into the depths, others climb toward the upper wings, and the panelled corridor runs back south.
Exits: down, north, south, up.
